## Working defaults

- Forms are data-driven by rows in `forms` and optional form packs under
  [`backend/app/forms/packs/`](mdc:backend/app/forms/packs). Field changes should
  usually be schema edits, not imperative code.
- A session stores a schema snapshot at creation time. Do not load the mutable
  current form schema while answering, reviewing, approving, or generating output
  for an existing session.
- Default run profile: `USE_MOCK_EMR=true`, no `OPENAI_API_KEY`; the rule-based
  fallback must keep working. Do not connect to a real EMR or model unless asked.
- AI provider wiring lives behind `backend/app/ai/llm.py`.
- Finish on the green bar: `cd backend; .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q`
  and `cd frontend; npm run build; npm run lint`. Add tests for behavior changes.
- Windows/PowerShell is the primary shell. App DB host port is `5499`.

## Scope guardrails

- Workflow tasks are explicit and fail closed. The supported tasks are
  `generate_pdf` and `web_submit`.
- `web_submit` requires a real recipe with `portal_url` before it can execute.
  The default mock driver is dry-run only.
- Keep PHI out of logs, model prompts, static KB, and agent docs.
